{
  "about": "Every price and sizing assumption behind /costs (the Simple Host Enterprise cost calculator), in one place. List prices in US dollars, excluding tax, on-demand (no commitments or discounts). Each price names the page it was read from and the day it was checked; scripts/check-prices-age.sh warns when any check is older than 45 days. costs/calc.js reads this file; nothing else holds a price.",
  "currency": "USD",
  "checked": "2026-09-28",
  "model": {
    "hours_per_month": 730,
    "replicas_min": 2,
    "page_views_per_replica": 5000000,
    "system_mem_gib": 1.0,
    "replica_mem_gib": 0.5,
    "upload_headroom_gib": 1.2,
    "node_reserved_gib": 0.75,
    "system_cpu": 0.5,
    "replica_cpu": 0.25,
    "versions_kept": 5,
    "replaced_versions_factor": 1.2,
    "db_base_gb": 1,
    "saved_data_factor": 3,
    "access_log_kb_per_view": 0.5,
    "access_log_months": 3,
    "db_mb_per_person": 1,
    "db_tiers_by_people": [[250, 1], [1000, 2], [5000, 4], [null, 8]],
    "db_min_tier_from_replicas": 3,
    "defaults": {
      "people": 100,
      "sites": 300,
      "views": 100000,
      "siteMB": 5,
      "savedMB": 1,
      "uploadsGB": 5,
      "viewMB": 1,
      "ha": false
    },
    "assumptions": [["Replicas", "The package runs 2 replicas of the service; we add one per 5 million page views a month. That rate is our assumption, not a load test: a replica serves sites from its own cache and does far more in practice."], ["Memory", "Each replica asks for 0.5 GiB (its request in the package). One upload at a time needs about 1.2 GiB more (UPLOAD_CONCURRENCY 2 × (100 MiB archive + 500 MiB unpacked)), and the ingress controller, cert-manager and the node's own agents about 1 GiB. Each node keeps 0.75 GiB for the system."], ["CPU", "Each replica asks for 0.25 CPU and the cluster's own pods about 0.5 CPU."], ["Nodes", "The cheapest mix of the provider's small general-purpose sizes that fits the memory and CPU above: 1 node, or at least 2 with high availability (3 on Hetzner, where k3s runs the control plane on the nodes). Our UpCloud trial ran 2 replicas, ingress and cert-manager on one 2 CPU / 4 GB node."], ["Database", "Sized by people: up to 250 on the ~1 GB plan, up to 1, 000 on ~2 GB, up to 5, 000 on ~4 GB, more on ~8 GB; at least ~2 GB from 3 replicas, since each replica opens up to 20 connections. High availability adds a standby in another zone."], ["Database storage", "1 GB, plus saved data × 3 (its history for undo), plus the access log (0.5 KB per page view, kept 90 days), plus 1 MB per person; never below the provider's smallest disk."], ["Bucket", "Every site keeps 5 versions (QUOTA_MAX_VERSIONS) at its average size, plus 20% for replaced versions the bucket keeps 30 days, plus uploaded files."], ["Traffic", "Page views × data sent per page view leave the cloud as internet egress. Uploads coming in are free everywhere. Traffic between the service, the bucket and the database stays inside one region."], ["Load balancer", "One load balancer in front of the ingress controller; on AWS a Network Load Balancer, charged per hour and per capacity unit (1 GB an hour processed)."], ["Per person", "The monthly total divided by the number of people who sign in."], ["Not included", "Tax, support plans, DNS, a NAT gateway (nodes here have public addresses), logs and metrics services, and commitment discounts, which lower most of these prices."]]
  },
